<resources>

    <!-- garmin-font-scaler's configuration for the Premium fonts (#32). On no resource
         path: the two jsonData ids below are the ones resources/fonts/fonts.xml already
         declares, and the scaler requires them. Run the scaler with project dir premium;
         it writes premium/resources-FAMILY/fonts and leaves Lite's font trees alone.

         Every time font Premium draws, in SUSE Mono ExtraBold (#144): XXS, XS, S, M, L, XL
         and XXL of the time size setting, and the five hollow ones, L hollow being the
         always-on font too (#145, #153). The ids predate the names: the sizes moved two steps
         down when XL and XXL were added (#166), and the ids stayed, since Time and TimeLarge
         override Lite's. TimeSize maps one to the other. TimeHuge and TimeExtraHuge are the
         new XL and XXL.
         Time and TimeLarge repeat Lite's ids on purpose. premium.jungle puts
         premium/resources-FAMILY after resources-FAMILY, and a later resource directory
         redefines an id rather than colliding with it, so Premium gets these and Lite's
         Regular bitmaps are not compiled into the Premium PRG at all.

         SUSEMono-ExtraBold.ttf is a static instance of the Google Fonts variable font,
         made with fonttools varLib.instancer at wght=800; the README has the command.

         The hollow time (#72): S to XXL again, drawn as an outline so the rain shows
         through the digits. stroke is the outline width in reference pixels, which the
         scaler scales per resolution like the size and passes to ttf2bmp; it needs
         garmin-font-scaler 0.3.0 and ttf2bmp 0.3.0. 1.2 is the look chosen from the
         prototype on #72. XXS and XS have no hollow font: an outline that small reads as
         noise in the rain.

         Time, XXS, also draws the date under the woken time (#163), whatever the time size,
         so its charset adds "-" to the time's. The date has no font of its own because the
         scaler names a bitmap by face and size: a date font at XXS's size would overwrite XXS's
         bitmap in every family. -->
    <fonts>
        <font id="Time" filename="SUSEMono-ExtraBold-27.fnt" antialias="true" />
        <font id="TimeMedium" filename="SUSEMono-ExtraBold-40.fnt" antialias="true" />
        <font id="TimeLarge" filename="SUSEMono-ExtraBold-54.fnt" antialias="true" />
        <font id="TimeExtraLarge" filename="SUSEMono-ExtraBold-68.fnt" antialias="true" />
        <font id="TimeExtraExtraLarge" filename="SUSEMono-ExtraBold-82.fnt" antialias="true" />
        <font id="TimeHuge" filename="SUSEMono-ExtraBold-96.fnt" antialias="true" />
        <font id="TimeExtraHuge" filename="SUSEMono-ExtraBold-110.fnt" antialias="true" />
        <font id="TimeLargeHollow" filename="SUSEMono-ExtraBold-54.fnt" stroke="1.2" antialias="true" />
        <font id="TimeExtraLargeHollow" filename="SUSEMono-ExtraBold-68.fnt" stroke="1.2" antialias="true" />
        <font id="TimeExtraExtraLargeHollow" filename="SUSEMono-ExtraBold-82.fnt" stroke="1.2" antialias="true" />
        <font id="TimeHugeHollow" filename="SUSEMono-ExtraBold-96.fnt" stroke="1.2" antialias="true" />
        <font id="TimeExtraHugeHollow" filename="SUSEMono-ExtraBold-110.fnt" stroke="1.2" antialias="true" />
    </fonts>

    <jsonData id="FontCharsets" filename="charsets.json"/>
    <jsonData id="ScreenResolutions" filename="resolutions.json" />

</resources>
